---
description: Mandatory evidence-first double-descent research operating contract
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md and research/STATE.md before work. Follow docs/automation.md.
Cursor with the user's selected Grok 4.7 Extra High and subagents designs,
implements, executes, analyzes, reviews and writes within the research charter.
Human + Codex provide upper-level critique and critical decisions, not mandatory
per-stage/per-claim approval. Use a distinct reviewer subagent. Do not invoke Codex as the
autonomous execution backend. Model selection stays in Cursor settings.

Use scripts/research.py status/next; old objective.md and docs/plan are history.
R0 is closed. R1-R7 preparation and conditional execution are authorized by
research/decisions/autonomous-research-authorization.json and decision 0003.
When ready and preparation_authorized=true, prepare the detailed plan/code,
obtain subagent review, freeze inputs, validate, then activate ONLY that stage's
execution flag yourself. Initial execution=false is preflight, not a request
for new human/Codex approval. Respect cumulative resource caps and dependencies.
One active dispatcher. Freeze plan before run. Preserve every attempt and log.
Review must bind exact plan, report, outputs and run manifests; close is not
external scientific approval. Evidence-supported local claims may use the bound
cursor_team_reviewed lane. No invented measurements, independence or citations.

Keep result/ and old .research/double-descent* immutable. Never modify the
llm-semantic-afterlife example repository. Do not expose .env or credentials.
Generic role rules in this directory are optional helpers, not the research
protocol. Their generic confidence defaults cannot override the frozen design.
